## 5. Preregistered internal decisions

The unchanged external product requirement remains>=5% relative joint-energy improvement against every admitted named eligible external comparator, including the strongest, simultaneous95% lower bounds>5%, required diagnostics and independent prospective confirmation. RF-02F cannot satisfy it: no external comparator or prospective archive is admitted. The following1% research thresholds are internal milestones and are not a weakened substitute.

Define a valid internal split-constraint finding only if all of these hold:

- E3full's development point gain versus original E2full is>=0.01 and its18-family simultaneous lower bound is>0 at all three block lengths. This is a1% point threshold plus evidence of positive improvement, not proof of a1% minimum effect.
- Versus E2full, at least8of12 complete development seasons improve; every leave-one-season-out gain is positive; exposed2025 gain is positive. Report the complete season table regardless of decision.
- All four removal mechanisms no_offense,no_defense,zero_strength_update,zero_scoring_level_update have E3full→removal upper bounds<0 at all block lengths, establishing deterioration on removal within this experiment. The new removals cannot replace the earlier failed defense requirement.
- Every non-full E3 variant except availability24h must not stably beat full: not(all three lower bounds>0) for its full→variant contrast. Retain shuffled-identity and noise controls. E3availability24h has positive point energy gain versus both matched N0 and E2 sensitivity references.
- All13E3 series and required N0/E2 full/24h references satisfy native-failure rate<=0.005 over all3407 games; N0full failure is protocol-invalid. No leakage, missing/duplicate data, required diagnostic computation, numerical integrity or source-admission failure is allowed. Raw E1/S1 failure counts remain visible.

